<title>HONG KONG: Cheung Kong 1996 net up 23.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Cheung Kong 1996 net up 23.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   602.0  vs  506.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    105.0  vs  90.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  1,514  vs  nil</p>
<p>    Net			   13,765  vs  11,125</p>
<p>    Turnover		    13,202  vs  12,309</p>
<p>    Company name		 Cheung Kong (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  May 29</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   May 30</p>
<p>NOTE - Cheung Kong (Holdings) is a major property developer in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 138 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 33 cents) vs 120 cents.</p>
<p>Turnover for 1995 has been restated to include income from infrastructure projects and to conform with 1996 turnover.</p>
<p>The exceptional item is a gain arising from the dilution of the group's interest through a placement and new issue of shares in Cheung Kong Infrastructure Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
